p("At the operating point selected by the false-alarm budget, FTT-IDS attains the highest mean F1 (93.65%) and accuracy (93.19%) and the lowest FPR among the five main comparators (4.44%). Table 4 places these differences in context. At τ_{FPR}(1%), FTT-IDS is significantly better than MLP (+0.85 F1 points), 1D-CNN (+0.75), FT-Transformer (+0.34) and the single-token control (+2.72), and marginally better than RF (+0.13, 95% CI [+0.02, +0.23]). It is statistically indistinguishable from XGBoost (+0.06, [−0.04, +0.16]). At τ = 0.5, by contrast, RF and XGBoost hold a small but significant advantage (−0.20 and −0.42 points). The feature-token Transformer is therefore competitive with, but not superior to, well-tuned gradient-boosted trees; this agrees with tabular-learning benchmarks {grinsztajn,shwartz}.")
