h2("4.4. Sensitivity to Test-Set Duplicates")
p("Table 8 repeats the UNSW-NB15 evaluation of representative models on the de-duplicated test set and on the de-duplicated test set without records whose feature vectors occur in the training file. Absolute scores fall, because the removed duplicates are predominantly easily detected attacks: the attack share drops from 55.1% to 38.9% and 37.6%, and FTT-IDS accuracy at τ = 0.5 falls from 87.2% to 83.1% and 83.0%. The conclusions are unchanged. The models remain within one F1 point of each other, and the false-alarm budget still lowers the FPR by about 21 points (to 4.6–4.7% for FTT-IDS) while raising accuracy to 90.6–90.8%. Results reported only on the official test file thus overstate absolute performance, but they rank models and decision rules consistently.")
